# A small shooter. Left and right move the ship, space fires, and at most three shots
# are in the air at once. Every shot is checked against every alien: that is the two
# sentences with "the same x and y" below.
#
#     ./intent run examples/shooter.intent        play it in a terminal
#     ./intent window examples/shooter.intent     play it in a window, in colour
#     ./intent build examples/shooter.intent && examples/shooter serve 8080
#                                                 the compiled game serves its own window

The board is 28 wide and 14 high.
The column starts at 14.
The score starts at 0.
The drift starts at 1.

Shots have an x and a y.
Aliens have an x, a y and a hit.

At the start there is an alien whose x is 4, whose y is 2 and whose hit is 0.
At the start there is an alien whose x is 8, whose y is 2 and whose hit is 0.
At the start there is an alien whose x is 12, whose y is 2 and whose hit is 0.
At the start there is an alien whose x is 16, whose y is 2 and whose hit is 0.
At the start there is an alien whose x is 20, whose y is 2 and whose hit is 0.
At the start there is an alien whose x is 6, whose y is 4 and whose hit is 0.
At the start there is an alien whose x is 10, whose y is 4 and whose hit is 0.
At the start there is an alien whose x is 14, whose y is 4 and whose hit is 0.
At the start there is an alien whose x is 18, whose y is 4 and whose hit is 0.

When left is pressed, decrease the column by 1 if the column is over 1.
When right is pressed, increase the column by 1 if the column is under 28.
When space is pressed, add a shot whose x is the column and whose y is 13 if the number of shots is under 3.

Every 60 milliseconds, decrease the y of the shots by 1.
Every 60 milliseconds, set the hit of the aliens to 1 if any shot has the same x and y.
Every 60 milliseconds, remove the shots that have the same x and y as an alien.
Every 60 milliseconds, increase the score by the number of aliens whose hit is 1.
Every 60 milliseconds, remove the aliens whose hit is 1.
Every 60 milliseconds, remove the shots whose y is under 1.

Every 400 milliseconds, increase the x of the aliens by the drift.
Every 400 milliseconds, set the drift to -1 if any alien has an x over 26.
Every 400 milliseconds, set the drift to 1 if any alien has an x under 3.
Every 5 seconds, increase the y of the aliens by 1.

The game is over when the number of aliens is 0.
The game is over when any alien's y is over 12.

Draw each alien as a green "W" at its x and y.
Draw each shot as a yellow "|" at its x and y.
Draw a cyan "A" at the column and 14.
Show the score above the board.
